1. **Original Scientific Value Definition**: This refers to the contribution of new methods, algorithms, theory, proofs, experimental findings, or novel analysis. The introduction section typically does not produce new scientific value—it serves to contextualize, motivate, and outline the paper. Therefore, **none of the segments create original scientific value** (i.e., all have zero new contributions).
   
