### Paragraph 2 (Text: "The second category of sampling techniques is **Sampling from Previous Layer**. This method selects nodes from earlier layers of the neural network to capture hierarchical dependencies and contextual information. It is effective for tasks requiring sequential data processing, such as time-series analysis or hierarchical classification problems. This approach has been used in models like the Temporal Convolutional Network (TCN) and in reinforcement learning frameworks."):

